* text=auto eol=lf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.png binary

# The guide ships inside the jar. A Windows checkout was rewriting it to CRLF,
# which cost 90 KB -- 5% of the plugin -- in carriage returns nobody reads.
*.json text eol=lf

# ...and it is 462,000 lines of it. Every regeneration rewrites the whole file.
#
# Marked binary for diffing only. The bytes committed and shipped are unchanged
# and the LF normalisation above still applies (checked: text set, eol lf, diff
# unset); git reports "1 file changed, 0 insertions(+), 0 deletions(-)".
#
# `linguist-generated=true` was tried instead and measured against the live hub
# commit: it collapses the diff in GitHub's web UI but still counts every line,
# giving 576,850 additions where `-diff` gives 8,765. A reviewer reading the web
# page sees the same either way; a review bot reading the API does not, and
# spending its budget on half a million lines of machine output is the problem
# this is here to solve.
#
# Nothing is hidden. The guide's diff is meant to be read in b0aty-guide-data,
# where the wiki sync opens a pull request against a pretty-printed copy and a
# person compares the steps before players see them.
src/main/resources/com/b0atyguide/guide.json -diff
